==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] in this stage aren't an issue as long as you have all [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]]. Even if you don't, [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] should be enough to completely stall them. For Shadow Boxer K, bring an [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark unit]] like [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]].

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The strategy for this stage will be very similar to what you used in Chapter 1, as the only enemy added is [[Kid  Tappa]], who has high health and speed, but deals almost no damage. You can still use Seafarer Cat and Pizza Cat to provide damage and crowd control, and use damage-dealers such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to quickly kill Kid Tappa, allowing your other units deal with the remaining enemies, which Awakened Bahamut can also do himself.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The third version of this stage introduces Scissoroos along with the enemies from the past versions, which can still be dealt with using Seafarer Cat, Pizza Cat, and other damage-dealers (e.g., Awakened Bahamut Cat). To hold off the new threat, you could also bring more meatshields, as the Scissoroos can push back your units. It's recommended to use nuker [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] if you have any, such as [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Merchant Babil]] or [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Yukimura]], to finish off the Shadow Boxer Ks and Scissoroos.

