==Trivia==
*In real life, [[wikipedia:Vega|Vega]] is the brightest star in the constellation of [[wikipedia:Lyra|Lyra]] as well as the 5th-brightest star in the night sky.
**The [[The Battle Cats|English]], Taiwanese, Korean, and [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese]] versions each have a different instrument as Vega's [[Treasure]]: a zither, a harp, a lyre and a koto, respectively. All of them are stringed instruments, presumably in reference to the constellation of Lyra.
*Vega on the [[Cats of the Cosmos]] map looks like a caricature of [[M. Bison (Uber Rare Cat)|M. Bison]], a ''[[Street Fighter Collaboration Event|Street Fighter]]'' character whose Japanese name is also Vega.
*The woman seen atop Vega's enemy base may be Orihime from the folktale of [https://youtu.be/GovtY2k4Jq4 Hikoboshi and Orihime] (''[[wikipedia:The Cowherd and the Weaver Girl|The Cowherd and the Weaver Girl]]''), star-crossed lovers identified as the stars [[wikipedia:Altair|Altair]] and Vega respectively.
**She may also be a reference to the Chinese legend of [[wikipedia:Chang'e|Chang'e]], which is about a young woman named Chang'e who ascended into the sky to become the goddess of the Moon.

